Synchronous global-header baseline and root cause
-------------------------------------------------
Baseline artifact SHA-256:
55da505e2b960cd4213f1b17320401e9c4aba1044a7ac2552be852ed6a7f6a34

The synchronous NDK H.264 encoder initialized c2.google.avc.encoder and
produced its first frame, then MP4 and Matroska encoding failed with
AVERROR_EXTERNAL. Raw H.264 completed, and asynchronous NDK encoding completed
with the same codec. Android logs reported Codec2 work completion status 95
and a MediaCodec UNKNOWN_ERROR.

FFmpeg's synchronous global-header path queued a dummy frame and EOS, flushed
the encoder, then queued the first real frame. Android defines flush recovery
for decoders while encoder behavior is undefined:
https://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaCodec#flush()

Patch 0002 sends synchronous NDK encoding through the existing
extract_extradata bitstream-filter path. This avoids the encoder flush and
matches the working asynchronous path. Patch 0003 adds checks for a NULL or
undersized encoder input buffer, propagates queue failures with their raw
status, and commits EOS state only after MediaCodec accepts it.

